    "notes": "Curated by hand for Spanish, seeded from the Spanish dictionary Story 6.1 shipped in community-moderation.engine.ts and extended to the category and severity model. Coverage spans the Peninsular, Mexican, Rioplatense, Chilean and Colombian registers the product serves. Every single-word term is at least four characters long, because each language's dictionary runs against every submission and a two or three character vulgarity in one language lands on an ordinary word in another; no entry here needed an exception to that floor. Entries that are also ordinary vocabulary in some register, such as capullo, hostia, polla and zorra, carry a low severity so a human reviewer makes the call on them. Hate slurs and self-harm incitement carry critical. Story 6.2b replaces this with a vendored, pinned upstream list under its own licence."
